<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Create Field From KML" dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormFieldKML`
    (FormFieldKML.cs + FormFieldKML.Designer.cs + FormFieldKML.resx). The operator types a
    new field name (sanitised live against glm.fileRegex), optionally appends the current date
    and/or time, picks a Google-Earth KML file whose outer <coordinates> ring becomes the field
    boundary, then saves — which creates the field directory + initial files and loads the KML
    boundary. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful parity reimplementation of the current Windows
    Forms look, never a redesign: no new colours, no relayout, no UX changes.

    This dialog is the close sibling of FormFieldDir ("Create New Field by name"); it is the same
    name/date/time pattern PLUS an extra "Load KML" button and a taller shell. The markup therefore
    deliberately follows the established, validated sibling view FormFieldDirView.axaml so the two
    dialogs stay visually and structurally consistent.

    Window shell — mirrors FormFieldKML.Designer.cs:
      ClientSize 608 x 332        -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window).
      FormBorderStyle.None        -> SystemDecorations="None".
      ControlBox = false          -> covered by the borderless (SystemDecorations="None") shell.
      ShowInTaskbar = false       -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      (Fixed, not resizable)      -> CanResize="False".
      StartPosition CenterParent  -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown modally over FormGPS;
                                     this replaces the WinForms ScreenHelper reposition, which per the
                                     file spec is intentionally NOT ported).
      Font Tahoma 14.25pt         -> FontFamily="Tahoma" + FontSize="19". WinForms points are converted
                                     to Avalonia device-independent pixels (pt x 96/72): 14.25 -> 19,
                                     18 -> 24. Because the window is sized 608 x 332 in DIP (1:1 with the
                                     WinForms client px), converting the fonts keeps the original physical
                                     proportions (same convention as the sibling FormFieldDirView).
      BackColor Gainsboro         -> Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}". Per this file's spec the
                                     neutral chrome is themed to the App.axaml day/night palette rather
                                     than hard-coding a WinForms colour.
      Text "Create New Field "    -> Title (design-time; the code-behind assigns gStr.gsCreateNewField).

    Wiring contract — the partner code-behind (FormFieldKMLView.axaml.cs) owns ALL behaviour:
      * Code-behind dialog: NO DataContext, NO x:DataType, NO MVVM bindings — exactly like the sibling
        FormFieldDirView / FormYesView / FormInputDialogView. Controls are addressed imperatively by
        their x:Name.
      * Button Click handlers are declared here (OnAddDateClick / OnAddTimeClick / OnLoadKmlClick /
        OnCancelClick / OnSaveClick) following the established OnXxxClick convention (e.g.
        FormYesView.axaml.cs: `private void OnOkClick(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)`). The code-behind
        implements them, reproducing btnAddDate_Click (append " yyyy-MM-dd" InvariantCulture),
        btnAddTime_Click (append " HH-mm" InvariantCulture), btnLoadKML_Click (KML OpenFileDialog ->
        FindLatLon + LoadKMLBoundary), btnSerialCancel_Click (Close) and btnSave_Click (save current
        field if a job is started, CreateNewField, LoadKMLBoundary, DialogResult OK, Close).
      * tboxFieldName declares NO events here: its TextChanged (glm.fileRegex sanitisation, then enable/
        disable btnLoadKML on a non-empty trimmed name) and its tap -> on-screen keyboard
        (FormGPS.isKeyboardOn) flow are attached in the code-behind by name, mirroring FormFieldKML.cs.
      * btnSave starts IsEnabled="False" (WinForms FormFieldDir_Load: btnSave.Enabled = false); the
        code-behind enables it only after a KML boundary loads successfully (LoadKMLBoundary sets
        btnSave.Enabled = true).
      * btnLoadKML starts enabled (its WinForms designer default — no Enabled=false is set); the
        code-behind disables it on an empty name and re-disables it after a successful load.
      * The "Enter Field Name" and "+" texts below are design-time placeholders; at runtime the
        code-behind assigns labelFieldname.Text = gStr.gsEnterFieldName.

    Colours come from App.axaml's day/night ThemeDictionaries via {DynamicResource ...} (so the live
    Light<->Dark switch is observed) — no WinForms colours, no GDI namespaces. Button glyphs are served
    from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs (BoundaryLoadFromGE / OK64 /
    Cancel64 / JobNameCalendar / JobNameTime) — the convention used by every sibling GPS view. The four
    OK/Cancel/Calendar/Time glyphs are native 64 x 64 PNGs; BoundaryLoadFromGE is a native 68 x 68 PNG
    (sized to its intrinsic dimensions below to avoid up/down-scaling).
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormFieldKMLView"
        Title="Create New Field"
        Width="608"
        Height="332"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="19"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}">

    <!--
        Flat, borderless, transparent image buttons — the cross-platform equivalent of the WinForms
        FlatStyle.Flat + FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + BackColor = Transparent carried by every button
        in FormFieldKML.Designer.cs. The Fluent Button template otherwise paints a hover / pressed /
        disabled fill; these setters keep the face transparent in all interaction states so only the
        glyph shows (the same technique used by the sibling FormFieldDirView and Keypad/NumKeypad).
        The :disabled face stays transparent too; the explicit Opacity below reproduces the greyed
        look of the WinForms disabled btnSave.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <!-- Disabled image buttons render their glyph dimmed, reproducing the greyed look WinForms
             applies to a disabled Button.Image (e.g. the initially-disabled btnSave). An Avalonia
             <Image> is unaffected by the Fluent theme's disabled foreground, so the dim is applied
             explicitly here via Opacity; it reverts to full opacity the moment the code-behind sets
             btnSave.IsEnabled = true after a KML boundary loads. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:disabled">
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Four logical bands (mirrors the designer's taller layout): the name label, the name textbox, the
        "+ date / + time" append band, and the bottom action band. Unlike the shorter FormFieldDir, the
        KML designer stacks these vertically inside the 332px height — the add buttons sit on their own
        row (y125-205) above a separate action row (y238-327) — so the layout uses four stacked rows
        rather than the sibling's two overlapping groups. The bottom action band places the "Load KML"
        button on the LEFT and the Cancel / Save buttons on the RIGHT, exactly as the designer positions
        them (btnLoadKML x=53, btnSerialCancel x=376, btnSave x=520).
    -->
    <Grid Margin="15,11,5,5">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- labelFieldname : designer (18,11)             -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- tboxFieldName  : designer (15,38) 565x36       -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- add band       : + date (left) + time          -->
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />      <!-- action band    : LoadKML (left) + Cancel/Save (right) -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- labelFieldname: Tahoma 14.25pt Bold (-> 19 DIP). Runtime text = gStr.gsEnterFieldName. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelFieldname"
                   Grid.Row="0"
                   Text="Enter Field Name"
                   FontSize="19"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                   Margin="0,0,0,6" />

        <!-- tboxFieldName: Tahoma 18pt Bold (-> 24 DIP), single line, stretched across the dialog
             (designer 565 wide). This is the focal control. Its TextChanged (sanitisation + btnLoadKML
             enable) and tap -> on-screen keyboard flow are wired in the code-behind, so no events are
             declared here. The WinForms BackColor (AliceBlue) is intentionally NOT hard-coded — the
             Fluent theme supplies the day/night-aware input background (no WinForms colours). -->
        <TextBox x:Name="tboxFieldName"
                 Grid.Row="1"
                 FontSize="24"
                 FontWeight="Bold"
                 MinHeight="44"
                 HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                 VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                 AutomationProperties.Name="Field name" />

        <!--
            Add band: the two "append to name" controls, each a "+" label followed by its image button
            (designer: label2 + btnAddDate, label3 + btnAddTime), left-aligned. btnAddDate appends the
            date (yyyy-MM-dd) and btnAddTime appends the time (HH-mm) — handled in the code-behind. The
            top margin reproduces the vertical gap the designer leaves below the textbox (y74 -> y125).
        -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="2"
                    Orientation="Horizontal"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                    Margin="0,18,0,0"
                    Spacing="40">

            <!-- + date -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                        Spacing="4"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <TextBlock x:Name="label2"
                           Text="+"
                           FontSize="19"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <Button x:Name="btnAddDate"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Width="83"
                        Height="79"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Add date"
                        Click="OnAddDateClick">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/JobNameCalendar.png"
                           Width="64"
                           Height="64"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- + time -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                        Spacing="4"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <TextBlock x:Name="label3"
                           Text="+"
                           FontSize="19"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <Button x:Name="btnAddTime"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Width="83"
                        Height="79"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Add time"
                        Click="OnAddTimeClick">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/JobNameTime.png"
                           Width="64"
                           Height="64"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

        </StackPanel>

        <!--
            Action band: Load KML (left) + Cancel/Save (right) share the bottom row.
            Designer x-order: btnLoadKML @ x=53, btnSerialCancel @ x=376, btnSave @ x=520 — all
            bottom-anchored. btnLoadKML opens the KML OpenFileDialog (code-behind); btnSave is enabled
            by the code-behind only after a boundary loads.
        -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="3">

            <!-- LEFT: Load KML (BoundaryLoadFromGE glyph, native 68 x 68). Starts enabled (designer
                 default); the code-behind disables it on an empty name / after a successful load. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnLoadKML"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Width="83"
                    Height="79"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                    VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Load KML"
                    Click="OnLoadKmlClick">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/BoundaryLoadFromGE.png"
                       Width="68"
                       Height="68"
                       Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- RIGHT: Cancel then Save (designer order), bottom-aligned. btnSave starts disabled
                 (WinForms FormFieldDir_Load) and is enabled by the code-behind after a KML load. -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                        VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                        Spacing="12">
                <Button x:Name="btnSerialCancel"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Width="77"
                        Height="79"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel"
                        Click="OnCancelClick">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                           Width="64"
                           Height="64"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnSave"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Width="83"
                        Height="79"
                        IsEnabled="False"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Save"
                        Click="OnSaveClick">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                           Width="64"
                           Height="64"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</Window>
